  "summary": "CLI tooling with benign network/base64 patterns; no installer-harm behavior observed",
  "details": "Package is an AI CLI tool. Static keyword matches appear in test files and policy templates: dist/services/codex-pre-tool-hook-template.test.js and codex-pre-tool-policy-template.js contain example/denylist strings referencing curl/wget/ping to placeholder hosts (example.com, evil.test, releases.hashicorp.com) consistent with pre-tool policy/safety rule fixtures rather than actual network calls. Buffer.from(..., 'base64').toString(...) usages in global-codex-config.js and release-preparation templates are standard config decoding, not dynamic code evaluation. templates/.agents/tools/runtime/api-mcp-runtime.mjs performs GET/POST operations as part of its documented MCP runtime. No lifecycle scripts fetch and execute remote code, no hardcoded attacker C2 endpoint is bound to a network call, no reads of installer credential stores (~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc, browser profiles) are present, and no environment scraping or exfiltration path is observed. The flagged tokens appear in test fixtures and policy template content rather than in reachable attack code.",
